sn12.20:1.5 | S: The Buddha said this: | T: The Blessed One said:
sn12.20:2.1 | S: “And what is dependent origination? | T: “Now what is dependent co-arising?
sn12.20:2.2 | S: Rebirth is a requirement for old age and death. | T: From birth as a requisite condition comes aging-&-death.
sn12.20:2.3 | S: Whether Realized Ones arise or not, this law of nature persists, this regularity of natural principles, this surety of natural principles, specific conditionality. | T: Whether or not there is the arising of Tathāgatas, this property stands—this regularity of the Dhamma, this orderliness of the Dhamma, this this/that conditionality.
sn12.20:2.4 | S: A Realized One awakens to this and comprehends it, | T: The Tathāgata directly awakens to that, breaks through to that.
sn12.20:2.5 | S: then he explains, teaches, asserts, establishes, clarifies, analyzes, and discloses it. | T: Directly awakening & breaking through to that, he declares it, teaches it, describes it, sets it forth. He reveals it, explains it, makes it plain,
sn12.20:2.6 | S: ‘Look,’ he says, | T: & says, ‘Look.’
sn12.20:2.7 | S: ‘Rebirth is a requirement for old age and death.’ | T: From birth as a requisite condition comes aging-&-death.
