sn12.20:3.8 | S: Consciousness is a requirement for name and form … | T: “From consciousness as a requisite condition comes name-&-form.…
sn12.20:3.9 | S: Choices are a requirement for consciousness … | T: “From fabrications as a requisite condition comes consciousness.…
sn12.20:3.10 | S: Ignorance is a requirement for choices. | T: “From ignorance as a requisite condition come fabrications.
sn12.20:3.11 | S: Whether Realized Ones arise or not, this law of nature persists, this regularity of natural principles, this surety of natural principles, specific conditionality. | T: Whether or not there is the arising of Tathāgatas, this property stands—this regularity of the Dhamma, this orderliness of the Dhamma, this this/that conditionality.
